              "note_id": "FCT_0275",
              "quote": "Students are asked to use what they have learned in this section to build a mortgage calculator."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "FCT_0276",
              "quote": "When the program runs, it asks a few questions."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "FCT_0277",
              "quote": "The first question asks for the principal, or the amount of loan."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "FCT_0278",
              "quote": "Example principal value: $100,000."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "FCT_0280",
              "quote": "Example interest rate: 3.92%."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "FCT_0013",
              "quote": "The third question asks for the period in years."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "FCT_0014",
              "quote": "Example period: 30 years."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "FCT_0281",
              "quote": "We need to multiply this number by 12 (months in a year) to calculate the number of payments."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "FCT_0286",
              "quote": "Monthly interest is calculated by taking the annual interest, dividing it by percent, and then dividing by months in a year."
            }
          ],
